    <div type="titlePage" canonical="false">
      <title type="main">Hebrew Gospels of Luke and John</title>
      <title type="sub">found in the Vatican Library</title>
      <title type="sub">Biblioteca Apostolica ebr. 530, part 1, fragment 11, folios 1r-2v</title>
      <title type="sub">Luke 1:1-35; John 1:1-13</title>
      <title type="sub">Transcribed, translated, and annotated by Nehemia Gordon</title>
      <title type="sub">with contributions by Keith Johnson and T-Bone</title>
      <title type="sub">Copyright 2018 Nehemia Gordon. All rights reserved. Version 3.9</title>
    </div>
    <div type="book" osisID="Luke" canonical="true">
        <chapter sID="Luke.1" osisID="Luke.1" n="1"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.1" osisID="Luke.1.1" n="1"/>In that many were placed to write the account of the matters that<verse eID="Luke.1.1"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.2" osisID="Luke.1.2" n="2"/>are trustworthy among us, without doubt, as they told them to us themselves, those who saw them from the beginning, and were my servants [of] the Word,<verse eID="Luke.1.2"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.3" osisID="Luke.1.3" n="3"/>it seemed also right to me, because from the beginning I sought all the things in order, to write to you with speed, dear Theophilo,<verse eID="Luke.1.3"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.4" osisID="Luke.1.4" n="4"/>in order that you would know the truth of the matter that you have learned.<verse eID="Luke.1.4"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.5" osisID="Luke.1.5" n="5"/>And it came to pass in the days of Herod, King of Judah, a certain Kohen, his name was Zechariah from the sons of Aviyah, and his wife from the children of Aaron<verse eID="Luke.1.5"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.6" osisID="Luke.1.6" n="6"/>and her name was Elisheva. And both of them were righteous before Yehovah and walking in all the statutes and judgements of Yehovah, without guile,<verse eID="Luke.1.6"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.7" osisID="Luke.1.7" n="7"/>and they did not have children; Elisheva was barren and both of them were<verse eID="Luke.1.7"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.8" osisID="Luke.1.8" n="8"/>advanced in years. And the Kohen Zechariah had the priesthood before Adona[i] Yehovah<note type="explanation" placement="foot" n="8" osisRef="Luke.1.8" osisID="Luke.1.8!note.8">The scribe apparently scratched out Adonai and replaced it with Yehovah.</note><verse eID="Luke.1.8"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.9" osisID="Luke.1.9" n="9"/>in the order of his family, according to the custom of the service of the priesthood.<verse eID="Luke.1.9"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.10" osisID="Luke.1.10" n="10"/>Yehovah and the multitudes of people were standing outside to pray at the time of the<verse eID="Luke.1.10"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.11" osisID="Luke.1.11" n="11"/>incense and the angel of Yehovah appeared to him, standing at right of the altar of<verse eID="Luke.1.11"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.12" osisID="Luke.1.12" n="12"/>incense and Zechariah, when he saw him, was<verse eID="Luke.1.12"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.13" osisID="Luke.1.13" n="13"/>terrified and fear seized hold of him. And the angel said to him “Do not fear, Zechariah, for your prayer is heard, and Elisheva your wife will give birth to<verse eID="Luke.1.13"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.14" osisID="Luke.1.14" n="14"/>the lot fell upon him to present the incense. And he came into the sanctuary of a son and you shall call his name Yochanan and there shall be to you joy and happiness<verse eID="Luke.1.14"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.15" osisID="Luke.1.15" n="15"/>the time of his birth, for he will be great before Yehovah and will not drink wine or strong drink<verse eID="Luke.1.15"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.16" osisID="Luke.1.16" n="16"/>and he will be filled from the Ru’ach HaKodesh from the womb of his mother and he will return many of the sons of Israel<verse eID="Luke.1.16"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.17" osisID="Luke.1.17" n="17"/>to Yehovah their Elohim and he will walk before him in the spirit and power of Eliyahu, to return the heart of the fathers to the sons and [he will return] the heretics to the righteousness of the<verse eID="Luke.1.17"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.18" osisID="Luke.1.18" n="18"/>and many will be happy at righteous ones and to prepare to Yehovah the people, prepared.” And Zechariah said to the angel, “How will I know this matter, for I am old and my wife<verse eID="Luke.1.18"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.19" osisID="Luke.1.19" n="19"/>is advanced in years?” And the angel answered and said, “I am Gabriel who stands before Yehovah and I was sent to speak to you and tell you these matters<verse eID="Luke.1.19"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.20" osisID="Luke.1.20" n="20"/>and behold, you will be mute and will not be able to speak until the day that these things are done, because you did not believe my words, that<verse eID="Luke.1.20"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.21" osisID="Luke.1.21" n="21"/>they would be fulfilled in their time.” And the people were waiting for Zechariah and wondering<verse eID="Luke.1.21"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.22" osisID="Luke.1.22" n="22"/>because of his delay in the sanctuary. And when he came out outside, he was not able to speak<verse eID="Luke.1.22"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.23" osisID="Luke.1.23" n="23"/>but remained a mute. And it came to pass when the days of his service were fulfilled and he went to<verse eID="Luke.1.23"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.24" osisID="Luke.1.24" n="24"/>his house and after these days, Elisheva his wife became pregnant. And she hid five months<verse eID="Luke.1.24"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.25" osisID="Luke.1.25" n="25"/>saying, “Why did Yehovah do this to me in the days that I see, to raise up my proverb among<verse eID="Luke.1.25"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.26" osisID="Luke.1.26" n="26"/>the people?” And in the sixth month, the angel Gabriel was sent from Yehovah in a city of the<verse eID="Luke.1.26"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.27" osisID="Luke.1.27" n="27"/>with them. And they knew he saw a vision in the sanctuary. And he was gesturing to them, Galilee, and its name was<verse eID="Luke.1.27"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.28" osisID="Luke.1.28" n="28"/>Miryam. And when the angel came to her he said, “Shalom to you, full of grace, Yehovah is with<verse eID="Luke.1.28"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.29" osisID="Luke.1.29" n="29"/>you,<note type="explanation" placement="foot" n="12" osisRef="Luke.1.29" osisID="Luke.1.29!note.12">The Hebrew is ambiguous and can mean “Yehovah is with you” or “Yehovah be with you”. The former is a statement, while the latter is a blessing. This ambiguity plays a key role in this passage as well as in Judges 6:12-13.</note> you are blessed among women.” And she looked and was frightened because of his words. And<verse eID="Luke.1.29"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.30" osisID="Luke.1.30" n="30"/>Natzaret, to a certain virgin who was betrothed to a man and his name was Yoseph from the House of David and the name of the virgin was she was thinking, “What sort of ‘Shalom’ was this?” And the angel said to her, “Do not fear, Miryam. For you have found favor before Yehovah.<verse eID="Luke.1.30"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.31" osisID="Luke.1.31" n="31"/>Behold you are<verse eID="Luke.1.31"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.32" osisID="Luke.1.32" n="32"/>pregnant and will give birth to a son and will call his name Yeshua. This one will be great and will be called Son of the Most High and Yehovah Elohim will give him the Throne of David<verse eID="Luke.1.32"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.33" osisID="Luke.1.33" n="33"/>his father and he will reign over the House of Ya’akov forever. And there will be no end<verse eID="Luke.1.33"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.34" osisID="Luke.1.34" n="34"/>to his kingdom.” And Miryam said to the angel, “How will this be,<verse eID="Luke.1.34"/>
        <verse sID="Luke.1.35" osisID="Luke.1.35" n="35"/>for I have not known a man?” And the angel answered and said to her, “The Ru’ach HaKadosh<note type="explanation" placement="foot" n="15" osisRef="Luke.1.35" osisID="Luke.1.35!note.15">The variant phrase Ru’ach HaKadosh רוח הקדוש (rather than the more common Ru’ach HoKodesh רוח הקודש, found above in verse 15) is attested with twenty instances in the Bar Ilan Responsa Database (version 24+). For example, Leviticus Rabbah 14:2.</note> will enter you and an exalted might will be in your shadow. Because he that will be born will be holy, he shall be called ‘Son of Yehovah.’”<verse eID="Luke.1.35"/>
        <chapter eID="Luke.1"/>
      </div>
  </osisText>
</osis>
